OHOS: keep the scrolled application and its controls visible during capture.
The compositor keeps the full-screen overlay opaque, so hide it during capture
instead of relying on a transparent hole. Detach the toolbar for the session so
auto-scroll remains reachable, keep the stitched preview alive as a parentless
top-level window, and delay the first frame until the overlay has been removed.
Reattach the toolbar when ordinary presentation resumes. Qt widget regressions
cover both the detached toolbar and the preview surviving their owner hiding.

